From: MacFinals
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: registry driver version, follow-up: unsigned int out-parameters

wine-wined3d-registry-driver-version.patch declared the out-parameters as DWORD, but
wined3d_driver_info's version_high/version_low are unsigned int; in the PE build DWORD is
unsigned long, so GCC rejected the call (-Wincompatible-pointer-types). The applied patch
can't change (WINE_PATCHES is append-only), so this follows it.

--- a/dlls/wined3d/directx.c	2026-11-25 13:33:23
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/directx.c	2026-11-25 13:33:23
@@ -747,7 +747,7 @@
  * minimum, DLSS hidden, asynchronous shader creation off), while DXGI and the registry report
  * the current one. Used only when exactly one display adapter is registered and its provider
  * matches VENDOR, so the version belongs to this GPU; otherwise the table stays. */
-static BOOL registry_driver_version(enum wined3d_pci_vendor vendor, DWORD *high, DWORD *low)
+static BOOL registry_driver_version(enum wined3d_pci_vendor vendor, unsigned int *high, unsigned int *low)
 {
     static const WCHAR class_key[] = L"System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Class\\"
             L"{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}";
